{"id":"2015489803068651120","kind":"article","title":"第二卷：如何真正改变你的想法","author":"Rob Bensinger","original_authors":["Rob Bensinger"],"original_source_urls":["https://www.readthesequences.com/Book-II-How-To-Actually-Change-Your-Mind"],"publisher":"Thoughts Memo","column":"理性 & 克服偏见","date":"2026-03-13","updated":"2026-07-22","votes":58,"comment_count":4,"minutes":1,"chars":434,"keywords":["动机性推理","确认偏误","自我欺骗","信念更新","理性"],"summary":"导言提出：人们为何反复坚持错误信念、难以修正观点，以及如何改进这一过程；随后概述《理性：从人工智能到僵尸》第二卷各系列，主题包括动机性推理、确认偏差、自欺和“像士兵一样争论”。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/2015489803068651120","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"E. 过于方便的借口"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"F. 政治与理性"},{"id":"sec-3","level":2,"title":"G. 反对合理化"},{"id":"sec-4","level":2,"title":"H. 反对双重思想"},{"id":"sec-5","level":2,"title":"I. 用新眼光看问题"},{"id":"sec-6","level":2,"title":"J. 死亡螺旋"},{"id":"sec-7","level":2,"title":"K. 放手"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"SKw9U2Rs\">看来“真实”这玩意儿似乎还挺好使的。那么，我们为什么会一遍又一遍地想当然，固执己见，一遍又一遍地犯下相同的错误呢？为什么我们如此不善于习得精确无误的信念，而又要如何才能做得更好？这七个系列讨论了动机性推理与确认偏差，尤其是难以察觉的自欺欺人和「像士兵一样争论」。</p><p data-pid=\"EwRbPdo4\">——<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.readthesequences.com/Biases-An-Introduction\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">《偏见：序言》</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>by Rob Bensinger</p><hr/><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-draft-cover=\"https://picx.zhimg.com/v2-52b323f664f6af45cbdffbe5bc602b8d.jpg?source=7e7ef6e2&amp;needBackground=1\" data-draft-title=\"理性：导读\" data-tm-id=\"827867654\" href=\"#/post/827867654\">理性：导读</a><h2 id=\"sec-1\">E. 过于方便的借口</h2><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-draft-cover=\"https://pic1.zhimg.com/v2-eb16b34c242bf59997738a371a8063ba.jpg?source=7e7ef6e2&amp;needBackground=1\" data-draft-title=\"过于方便的借口\" data-tm-id=\"991304319\" href=\"#/post/991304319\">过于方便的借口</a><h2 id=\"sec-2\">F. 政治与理性</h2><a class=\"internal tm-internal\" data-draft-cover=\"https://pica.zhimg.com/v2-db9af3f23d2